>compEquiv</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LinearEquiv</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">trans_symm</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LinearEquiv</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">symm_symm</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Basis</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">baseChange_apply</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LinearMap</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">coe_comp</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LinearEquiv</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">coe_coe</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LinearMap</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">coe_inr</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Function</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">comp_apply</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LinearEquiv</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">trans_apply</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Basis</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">repr_symm_apply</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pderiv_X</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">toComp_val</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Basis</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">repr_linearCombination</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LinearMap</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">liftBaseChange_tmul</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">one_smul</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">repr_CotangentSpaceMap</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">obtain</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;;&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Basis</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">prod_repr_inr</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Basis</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">baseChange_repr_tmul</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">Basis</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">repr_self</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Basis</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">prod_repr_inl</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">map_zero</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finsupp</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">coe_zero</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">Pi</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">zero_apply</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ne_eq</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">not_false_eq_true</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Pi</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">single_eq_of_ne</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Pi</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">single_apply</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">Finsupp</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">single_apply</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ite_smul</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">one_smul</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">zero_smul</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Sum</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">inr</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">injEq</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">MonoidWithZeroHom</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">map_ite_one_zero</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">reduceCtorEq</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">end</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bad_universes</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n</div></div>\n<p>Unfortunately, the core people really need a mathlib-free minimisation of this file to debug, and this file begins <code>import Mathlib.RingTheory.Kaehler.JacobiZariski</code>. The challenge is to minimise this file to be mathlib-free before all the comments in the file about timings stop being true.</p>\n<p>In short: how do we minimise a file from deep in mathlib to a core Lean file, within (say) 1 week?</p>",
        "id": 591997556,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1777539996
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Oh I should add: Kim has stressed to me that it's important to have <code>#guard_msgs</code> commands in a minimisation challenge, because it's important to know that any changes made to the file preserve the phenomenon that you are trying to minimise. But I do not know how to change Lean so that it times out if the kernel takes 25M mHeartbeats to typecheck something. Can someone fill me in? I can then edit the code above to ensure that any attempt to use the minimiser will be useful.</p>",
        "id": 591999836,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1777540672
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"110038\">Kevin Buzzard</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Minimisation.20challenge.3A.20a.20race.20against.20time.2E/near/591999836\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>But I do not know how to change Lean so that it times out if the kernel takes 25M mHeartbeats to typecheck something.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Just to clarify here, your point is that taking too many heartbeats in <strong>elaboration</strong> is easy to check for using <code>set_option maxHeartbeats X in</code>, and then a <code>#guard_msgs</code> that expected the out-of-heartbeats message, but you don't know how to do something equivalent for slow kernel checks?</p>",
        "id": 592021466,
        "sender_full_name": "Kim Morrison",
        "timestamp": 1777546730
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>set_option trace.profiler true</code> will output something called <code>Lean.addDecl</code>, and in there there's a number for how long the kernel takes to typecheck the thing. It's not an exact timeout, but that's how I personally investigate kernel slowdowns.</p>",
        "id": 592056460,
        "sender_full_name": "Bhavik Mehta",
        "timestamp": 1777555951
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Just having output is not good enough: it has to be checkable via #guard_msgs (or some relative that we add, e.g. #guard_panic required a slightly different mechanism).</p>",
        "id": 592058653,
        "sender_full_name": "Kim Morrison",
        "timestamp": 1777556459
    }
]